activation	Print prompt	2026-10-28T05:00:54.0769852Z {"title": "FPE crash when progress bar enabled", "body": "### What happens?\n\nWhen using the DuckLake and SQLite extensions, DuckDB crashes when the progress bar is enabled and runs OK when it is not\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```\n.timer on\n\nPRAGMA disable_progress_bar; --enable this to cause crash\nPRAGMA explain_output='all';\n\nINSTALL ducklake;\nLOAD ducklake;\nINSTALL sqlite;\nLOAD sqlite;\n\nSET memory_limit='1GB';\nSET threads=1;\nSET temp_directory='./tempfiles';\n\nATTACH 'ducklake:sqlite:metadata.sqlite' AS dl (DATA_PATH 'data_files/');\n\nCREATE TABLE dl.metars AS SELECT * FROM read_parquet('../raw_metars') LIMIT 0;\n\nALTER TABLE dl.metars SET PARTITIONED BY (YEAR(timeObs), MONTH(timeObs));\nALTER TABLE dl.metars SET SORTED BY (stationName ASC, timeObs ASC);\n\nCALL dl.set_option('parquet_compression', 'zstd');\nCALL dl.set_option('parquet_compression_level', 12);\n\nINSERT INTO dl.metars SELECT * FROM read_parquet('../raw_metars/') ;\n```\n\nWhen I `cat` this into duckdb, eg `cat create.sql | duckdb`\n\n\nProduces this crash when I run it with gdb:\n\n```Thread 1 \"duckdb\" received signal SIGFPE, Arithmetic exception.\n0x0000000000894cc7 in duckdb_shell::ShellProgressBarDisplay::PrintProgressInternal(int, double, bool) ()\n(gdb) bt\n#0  0x0000000000894cc7 in duckdb_shell::ShellProgressBarDisplay::PrintProgressInternal(int, double, bool) ()\n#1  0x000000000095e108 in duckdb::TerminalProgressBarDisplay::Update(double)\n    ()\n#2  0x000000000095a605 in duckdb::ProgressBar::Update(bool) ()\n#3  0x0000000000d6e8c5 in duckdb::ClientContext::ExecuteTaskInternal(duckdb::ClientContextLock&, duckdb::BaseQueryResult&, bool) ()\n#4  0x0000000000d6eaac in duckdb::PendingQueryResult::ExecuteInternal(duckdb::ClientContextLock&) ()\n#5  0x0000000000d6ec56 in duckdb::PendingQueryResult::Execute() ()\n#6  0x0000000000d72b10 in duckdb::ClientContext::Query(duckdb::unique_ptr<duckdb::SQLStatement, std::default_delete<duckdb::SQLStatement>, true>, duckdb::QueryParameters) ()\n#7  0x0000000000d7356d in duckdb::Connection::SendQuery(duckdb::unique_ptr<duckdb::SQLStatement, std::default_delete<duckdb::SQLStatement>, true>, duckdb::QueryParameters) ()\n#8  0x000000000085bd13 in duckdb_shell::ShellState::ExecuteStatement(duckdb::unique_ptr<duckdb::SQLStatement, std::default_delete<duckdb::SQLStatement>, true>) ()\n#9  0x000000000085c017 in duckdb_shell::ShellState::ExecuteSQL(std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char> > const&) ()\n#10 0x000000000085c31b in duckdb_shell::ShellState::RunOneSqlLine(duckdb_shell::InputMode, char*) ()\n#11 0x0000000000866e8e in duckdb_shell::ShellState::ProcessInput(duckdb_shell::InputMode) ()\n#12 0x000000000086827e in RunShell(int, char const**) ()\n#13 0x00000000008388df in main ()```\n\n### OS:\n\n`$ uname -a Linux oriskany 6.14.0-29-generic #29~24.04.1-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu Aug 14 16:52:50 UTC 2 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux`\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\nv1.5.2 (Variegata) 8a5851971f\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nCLI\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nJohn Jensen\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nNone\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nNo - I cannot easily share my data sets due to their large size"}
